{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "coordinateSystem": "Original atlas pixels; top-left origin. Export converts points to each alpha-bounded rect, normalized bottom-left origin.",
  "status": "Source-image joint registration implemented; Unity producer visual acceptance pending.",
  "notes": [
    "Points are explicit per source image, visually registered to sleeve openings, palms, chin/nape/neck bases and torso collar openings; they are not inferred from alpha bounding-box ratios.",
    "Side heads face east. Eleven side torsos face west in the original art; only the protagonist side torso already faces east. mirrorX normalizes only the torso and its sockets.",
    "Protagonist and guard torso meshes omit baked sleeves/upper arms while retaining shoulder overlap, collar, belt and lower garment. Original PNG pixels and GUIDs remain unchanged.",
    "Front/back head pivots retain their existing chin/nape registration. Side heads register a short-neck cross-section at the torso collar; explicit visible meshes remove the extra painted collar or lower bare neck while retaining long hair and beard branches. Existing worldHeight values are retained.",
    "leftShoulderSocket/rightShoulderSocket name the far/near arm for side views, and screen-left/screen-right arm for front/back views. Side socket source points are reflected with mirrorX before assembly.",
    "The protagonist right-arm logical part 2 explicitly mirrors the calibrated left-arm part 3. The original two PNG arms have the same thumb handedness; aliasing gives symmetric sleeves, pivots and palms without repainting or replacing source pixels."
  ],
